// Relational predicates — the vocabulary goals are expressed over. A predicate is
// a relation that holds (or not) of an entity: `enthroned(e)` is true of whoever
// rules; `alive(e)` of whoever lives. Goals are conditions on these (e.g. "make
// enthroned(self) true", "make alive(foe) false"); the planner grounds each one to
// a flat fact slot per agent. Add a predicate here and a goal can name it.
[
    "enthroned",
    "alive",
    // The achlydesan facts — a soul's standing in the Demiurge's order. No *bundled* goal
    // targets these, so they perturb no economy; they are the vocabulary the Archon Law
    // (norms.ron) regulates and that scenarios and the deeper layers reason over.
    "awakened", // has the soul woken to the truth of the world? (gnosis, made fact)
    "bound",    // is the soul chained to the wheel of fate — marked, in the Archons' ledger?
    "ascended", // has the soul passed the seven and risen out of the counterfeit?
    // Further facts the deeper layers (norms, scenarios) reason over — a soul's standing in
    // the chronicle of the dead.
    "marked",     // singled out by an Archon's hand — branded for the wheel
    "hallowed",   // set apart as holy by the cult
    "cursed",     // damned by name
    "remembered", // named and held against the forgetting
    "exiled",     // cast out of every faction and hearth
]
